    url: "https://x.com/ZentrixHQ/status/2083527804201615507",
    postedAt: "2026-08-01",
    views: 3776,
    likes: 25,
    text: "📖A feature buried in the Seedance 2.5 release notes is quietly solving the problem every AI filmmaker complains about. Most people are celebrating the 30-second clips and the 3-minute long mode. The actual game-changer is easy to miss. Seedance 2.5 accepts up to 50 multimodal references in a single generation - including 3D white models and green-screen footage. That means a rough 3D block-out or a real green-screen shot can be dropped in as a reference, and the model builds the final scene around it instead of guessing the composition from a text prompt alone. The lifehack: stop writing longer prompts to get exact camera angles or character poses. Build a cheap 3D white model of the shot instead - even a rough one - feed it in as a reference, and let Seedance 2.5 handle the lighting, texture, and detail on top of a composition that's already locked. The upgrade that matters isn't the length. It's that Seedance 2.5 stopped being a text-to-video tool and started accepting real production assets as input. 📥Tomorrow I will talk about another feature that not everyone uses.",
