    postedAt: "2026-08-03",
    views: 144,
    likes: 0,
    text: "I think one of the biggest reasons people get inconsistent results with Seedance 2.5 isn't the model. It's that they're prompting it like every other video model. After going through ByteDance's official documentation, a few things stood out. Seedance clearly expects prompts to be structured differently. It separates reference roles, breaks actions into sequential stages, pays much more attention to temporal continuity, and even has its own conventions for handling audio and dialogue. In other words... It's less about writing a creative prompt. It's more about describing a scene the way the model actually understands it. I think this is becoming a broader trend across AI. The best results no longer come from finding a magical prompt. They come from understanding how each model \"thinks\" and adapting your workflow accordingly. If you're using Seedance 2.5, these two official guides are absolutely worth reading before your next generation. 📖 User Guide: https://t.co/uKs7iu7Jzx 📖 Prompt Guide: https://t.co/tsYeEeZ30W",
