    likes: 44,
    text: "I used ChatGPT to analyse a Fast & Furious chase scene and turn it into better Seedance 2.5 prompts. The difference was huge. I was prompting “high-speed chase”, but the shots still felt slow, not dynamic at all. So I had chat gpt (5.6 Sol on High) study and analyze a reference clip and pull out the actual visual cues of speed: • start already at full speed • let the camera get overtaken • use strong foreground parallax • let vehicles rapidly change size in frame • vary the distance between the vehicles • use short interior inserts as punctuation • reveal hazards late I then gave ChatGPT ByteDance’s official Seedance prompting guide and asked it to audit the prompt. https://t.co/XmU5nvXkbv Chat GPT revised the prompts around the Bytedance guidance, simplifying the physical action, separating it from the camera direction, and giving each clip one clear action arc. As you can see from the side-by-side, the camera work shares the same visual language, and it worked well. To note, my version is several shorter generations edited together, rather than one continuous generation. The full caht GPT analysis prompt is in next post below 👇",
