    postedAt: "2026-08-04",
    views: 220,
    likes: 8,
    text: 'Step 1 Use ChatGPT to reverse-engineer your reference clip. It will break down the camera grammar, editing rhythm, geography and visual energy, then turn the analysis into reusable Seedance 2.5 prompt blocks: "Analyze this reference clip like an action editor, cinematographer, stunt coordinator and prompt engineer. I want to use the clip as reference for building an AI video prompt. Important: - Keep the physical action description plain, literal and easy to visualise. - Put the cinematic detail into the camera, speed, composition and atmosphere blocks. - Focus especially on how the scene creates perceived speed and impact. Please return: 1. A simple description of what physically happens 2. The main visual cues that create speed and intensity 3. A breakdown of the camera language 4. A breakdown of the editing rhythm 5. A breakdown of the geography and subject positioning 6. A breakdown of the composition style 7. The most useful extracted lessons 8. Reusable prompt blocks under these headings: - Action - Camera - Speed - Composition - Environment - Sound The goal is to produce prompt language that is practical and reusable, not just scene analysis."',
