    likes: 0,
    text: "12 locations and one face. That was the entire input for this poetry short film. Here's what I did with the new Seedance 2.5! 🎬 Here's what I learned that you can use tomorrow: → Generate your base locations in @magnific with Flux model by @bfl_ai. Empty location plates give the model geography and let you direct the performance in the prompt. → One headshot is enough for character consistency a lot of times. Not a 20-image character sheet. One clean front-on reference, carried across 13 total refs into a 30-second generation. → Everything cinematic lives in the prompt, not the reference. Lens, camera move, grain, framing, depth of field, blocking, time of day. If it's in the plate you can't change it. If it's in the prompt you can iterate it for free. → Generate long, not short. Two 30-second generations instead of twelve 5-second clips now using Seedance 2.5 by @BytedanceTalk. The model holds its own internal cuts, and you inherit continuity instead of engineering it. → Vary your angles or it reads AI. Grass-level low angle, static landscape wide, handheld follow-behind, one anamorphic iris. Uniform camera height is the single loudest generative tell. → Put extras in your plates. Empty streets read synthetic. One pedestrian fixes a shot. Poem: Whitney Hanson, \"I Sit in a Field Between My Past and My Future.\" Score: Arcade Fire & Owen Pallett, from Her — music written for a film about a man in love with an AI, now scoring a film made with one. Not planned. Seedance 2.5 is at 720p because 720p is the only option right now on @dreamina_ai. It won't be for long! 🤞 The model isn't the bottleneck anymore. Knowing what a shot is for is. Made with @magnific & @dreamina_ai ✨ (Comment for full prompts) #AIFilmmaking #Seedance #GenerativeAI #Cinematography #Magnific #newseedance #poetry #shortfilm #AIvideo #dreaminaAI",
